From 149cc513fa5246cc8e715877d62cfa42fcac55a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Wu <eric3u@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:13:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] MdeModulePkg/DisplayEngineDxe: Follow a language change
 without a reboot

The display engine and CustomizedDisplayLib look their strings up once,
when they load, and keep them: the key help, the pop-ups, the status bar
and the help of the F9/F10 hot keys, which the engine registers with the
browser. A language picked in the front page therefore reaches only the
forms themselves, while everything around them stays in the language the
system booted in until the next reboot.

Take the strings again when PlatformLang differs from the one they were
taken in, checked each time a form is displayed. The hot keys are
registered again as well; the browser keeps its own copy of their help
and refuses a key it already has, so the old registration is dropped
first. The browser copies the hot keys into each form before showing it,
so their help follows from the next form on; the language is picked on
the front page, which has no hot keys, so this is not noticeable.

Signed-off-by: Eric Wu <eric3u@outlook.com>
